  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "complete-v",
      "finish-v"
    ],
    "note": "**Finish** is the usual word in conversation: *Have you finished your dinner?* **Complete** is more formal and is used especially for work, studies, and official tasks: *complete a degree*. Only **finish** is followed by an **-ing** form: *finish reading*."
